USB MIDI host, the platform's side: an app switches the USB-C port between a device (the computer's) and the host of
a USB-MIDI controller (plat.h plat_usb_host, plat_usb_host_state, plat_usb_host_event), with FM1B_USB_HOST 1 in its
app.h (default 0: nothing of it is built). The main loop runs the driver's uh_task; the host simulator has the same
API and a "usbhost plug | nomidi | unplug" command. The driver is felucca-bsp's chip/usb_host.c
(patches/felucca-bsp/0002-usb-midi-host.patch), from Melodee pull request #75 by Adrien Tibi (Recursive Field
Instruments), under MPL-2.0 by its author's leave (quoted in that patch and in the driver's header:
https://github.com/keremimo/melodee/pull/75#issuecomment-6384184014). This patch is ignis32's (MPL-2.0).
Why MIDIMON needs it: a USB-MIDI controller plugged into the FM-1 itself, monitored and passed on by THRU.
Applies to: fm1-base aa2b3bc. Upstream: keremimo means to bring USB host to fm1-base (same thread).
